<div id=3D"S3.p2" class=3D"ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id=3D"S3.p2.1" class=3D"ltx_p" data-imt-p=3D"1"><span id=3D"S3.p2.1.1" c=
lass=3D"ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Scaling principle.</span>
Conventionally, the relationship between accuracy and efficiency in model p=
erformance is characterized as a =E2=80=9Ctrade-off=E2=80=9D, with a typica=
l preference for accuracy at the expense of efficiency. In pursuit of this,=
 numerous methods have been proposed with cumbersome operations. Point Tran=
sformers &nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href=3D"http=
s://arxiv.org/html/2312.10035?_immersive_translate_auto_translate=3D1#bib.b=
ib106" title=3D"" class=3D"ltx_ref">106</a>, <a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/h=
tml/2312.10035?_immersive_translate_auto_translate=3D1#bib.bib90" title=3D"=
" class=3D"ltx_ref">90</a>]</cite> prioritize accuracy and stability by sub=
stituting matrix multiplication in the computation of attention weights wit=
h learnable layers and normalization, potentially compromising efficiency. =
Similarly, Stratified Transformer&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacr=
o_cite">[<a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.10035?_immersive_translate_=
auto_translate=3D1#bib.bib40" title=3D"" class=3D"ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite> a=
nd Swin3D&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href=3D"http=
s://arxiv.org/html/2312.10035?_immersive_translate_auto_translate=3D1#bib.b=
ib101" title=3D"" class=3D"ltx_ref">101</a>]</cite> achieve improved accura=
cy by incorporating more complex forms of relative positional encoding, yet=
 this often results in decreased computational speed.<font class=3D"notrans=
late immersive-translate-target-wrapper" lang=3D"zh-CN" style=3D""><br><fon=
t class=3D"notranslate immersive-translate-target-translation-theme-none im=
