<div id=3D"S5.SS2.p7" class=3D"ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id=3D"S5.SS2.p7.1" class=3D"ltx_p" data-imt-p=3D"1"><span id=3D"S5.SS2.p=
7.1.1" class=3D"ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model efficiency.</span> We evaluat=
e model efficiency based on average latency and memory consumption across r=
eal-world datasets. Efficiency metrics are measured on a single RTX 4090, e=
xcluding the first iteration to ensure steady-state measurements. We compar=
ed our PTv3 with multiple previous SOTAs. Specifically, we use the NuScenes=
 dataset to assess outdoor model efficiency (see Tab.&nbsp;<a href=3D"https=
://arxiv.org/html/2312.10035?_immersive_translate_auto_translate=3D1#footno=
te2" title=3D"Footnote 2 =E2=80=A3 Table 1 =E2=80=A3 3 Design Principle and=
 Pilot Study =E2=80=A3 Point Transformer V3: Simpler, Faster, Stronger" cla=
ss=3D"ltx_ref"><span class=3D"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) and the S=
canNet dataset for indoor model efficiency (see Tab.&nbsp;<a href=3D"https:=
//arxiv.org/html/2312.10035?_immersive_translate_auto_translate=3D1#S5.T11.=
fig1" title=3D"Table 11 =E2=80=A3 5.2 Results Comparision =E2=80=A3 5 Exper=
iments =E2=80=A3 Point Transformer V3: Simpler, Faster, Stronger" class=3D"=
ltx_ref"><span class=3D"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>). Our results d=
emonstrate that PTv3 not only exhibits the lowest latency across all tested=
 scenarios but also maintains reasonable memory consumption.<font class=3D"=
