<p id=3D"A1.SS1.p3.1" class=3D"ltx_p" data-imt-p=3D"1"><span id=3D"A1.SS1.p=
3.1.1" class=3D"ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Other Downstream Tasks.</span>
We outline our configurations for indoor instance segmentation and outdoor =
object detection in Tab.&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.10035?=
_immersive_translate_auto_translate=3D1#A1.T14" title=3D"Table 14 =E2=80=A3=
 Appendix A Implementation Details =E2=80=A3 Point Transformer V3: Simpler,=
 Faster, Stronger" class=3D"ltx_ref"><span class=3D"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1=
4</span></a>. For indoor instance segmentation, we use PointGroup&nbsp;<cit=
e class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/=
2312.10035?_immersive_translate_auto_translate=3D1#bib.bib35" title=3D"" cl=
ass=3D"ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite> as our foundational framework, a popular cho=
ice in 3D representation learning&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacr=
o_cite">[<a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.10035?_immersive_translate_=
auto_translate=3D1#bib.bib94" title=3D"" class=3D"ltx_ref">94</a>, <a href=
=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.10035?_immersive_translate_auto_translate=
=3D1#bib.bib30" title=3D"" class=3D"ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href=3D"https://arx=
iv.org/html/2312.10035?_immersive_translate_auto_translate=3D1#bib.bib91" t=
itle=3D"" class=3D"ltx_ref">91</a>, <a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.=
10035?_immersive_translate_auto_translate=3D1#bib.bib92" title=3D"" class=
=3D"ltx_ref">92</a>]</cite>. Our configuration primarily follows PointContr=
ast&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href=3D"https://ar=
xiv.org/html/2312.10035?_immersive_translate_auto_translate=3D1#bib.bib94" =
title=3D"" class=3D"ltx_ref">94</a>]</cite>, with necessary adjustments mad=
e for PTv3 compatibility. Regarding outdoor object detection, we adhere to =
the settings detailed in FlatFormer&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citema=
cro_cite">[<a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.10035?_immersive_translat=
e_auto_translate=3D1#bib.bib51" title=3D"" class=3D"ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite>=
 and implement CenterPoint as our base framework to assess PTv3=E2=80=99s e=
ffectiveness. It=E2=80=99s important to note that PTv3 is versatile and can=
 be integrated with various other frameworks due to its backbone nature.<fo=
